From b0a59ffb77464aab66b36ffb1d670b1af3c81a86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TuNV <steven.nguyen.bn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 13:16:05 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] [icwmp P4 fix] wlan_mtk.c: a wildcard in a comment closed it
 early

"mlo_sync_*/backhaul_sync_*" ends the block comment at the first "*/", so
the rest of the line became code and the definition of wlan_sync_option()
after it was lost:

  wlan_mtk.c:181: error: unknown type name 'backhaul_sync_'
  wlan_mtk.c:234: warning: implicit declaration of wlan_sync_option

Comment reworded, no code change.

Also const-qualified the MTK config helpers (mtk_uci, mtk_varstate,
mtk_varstate_set, mtk_uci_default) and dropped const from the wan_entry
pointer inside wanip_mtk.c, which removes every -Wdiscarded-qualifiers the
build reported without touching the engine's dmuci API.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
